<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE electron-iqps9 ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Electron &#x27;The Sea God Surveys&#x27; (iQPS Launch 9) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Loft: Rocket Lab Electron Payload User Guide 8.0 GENERIC example flight profile (not this mission): altitude knots 0@0s, ~78km@155s (S1 cutoff),
~82km@162s (S2 ignition), ~126km@184s (fairing sep); S2 cutoff L+535s. Source: https://rocketlabcorp.com/assets/Rocket-Lab-Electron-Payload-User-Guide-8.0.pdf
Rocket Lab has published NO timeline for The Sea God Surveys (https://rocketlabcorp.com/missions/launches/iqps-the-sea-god-surveys/ : NET 3 Nov NZ, launch time TBD).
Assumptions: (a) S2-cutoff altitude set to iQPS&#x27;s 575 km target orbit (https://i-qps.net/en/news/4118/), altitude linear 184s-&gt;535s;
(b) ground-relative horizontal speed ramps linearly 0 -&gt; 7.228 km/s (circular v at 575 km minus Earth rotation along Az) at 535s.
Real Electron parks in a lower elliptical orbit and the Kick Stage circularizes later (timing unpublished); this file ends at S2 cutoff.
Azimuth: mean bearing from LC-1 to NOTAM debris-area centroids B5324/26 NZD032 -40.88,-174.78 (108.3 deg) and B5325/26 NZD033 -42.02,-159.45 (106.4 deg)
(HYDROPAC 3128/26, 3129/26 same areas; NOTAM B5323/26 launch window 2611021600-1820Z). https://www.space-notices.com/ . Inclination unpublished (&#x27;mid-inclined&#x27;, iQPS).
Payload: 1x QPS-SAR-20 &#x27;WADATSUMI-II&#x27; (iQPS 9). T0: LL2 NET 2026-11-02T16:41:00Z (Mon 2 Nov 8:41 am PST), window 16:00-18:20Z, status Go (LL2 update 2026-10-31T13:53Z).
Pad (LL2): -39.262833N 177.864469E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=107.38 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-02T16:41:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
